# Project Overview & Conventions

Pincushion is a popup for saving bookmarks to Pinboard, built with React, TypeScript and Redux Toolkit, bundled by Vite and tested with Vitest. It talks to Pinboard through the pinboard-bridge proxy (see `VITE_PINBOARD_BRIDGE_URL` in `.env`).

## Key Directories:

*   **`src/`**: The application source.
    *   The entry point is [src/index.tsx](mdc:src/index.tsx); [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx) orchestrates the lookups.
    *   **`src/redux/`**: Slices, selectors and the store, e.g. [src/redux/bookmarkSlice.ts](mdc:src/redux/bookmarkSlice.ts).
    *   **`src/components/`**: React components.
    *   **`src/services/`**: Calls to the bridge and to OpenAI.
    *   **`src/utils/`**: Pure helpers and the localStorage caches.
    *   **`src/styles/`**: The popup stylesheet (good-css conventions: OKLCH `light-dark()` tokens, logical properties).

## Testing Strategy:

*   Vitest with React Testing Library; `npm test` runs everything.
*   Most tests live in [src/__testing__](mdc:src/__testing__) (app, redux) and in `__tests__` folders beside components, services and utils; a few sit beside their source as `*.test.ts(x)`. Vitest picks up all three.
*   Also run `npm run lint`, `npm run lint:css` and `npm run build` (which type-checks) before pushing; CI runs all of them.

